header><strong class=3D"style_chapter__grtAe">26</strong><h1>Real-time Gami=
ng Leaderboard</h1></header><p>In this chapter, we are going to walk throug=
h the challenge of designing a leaderboard for an online mobile game.</p>
<p>What is a leaderboard? Leaderboards are common in gaming and elsewhere t=
o show who is leading a particular tournament or competition. Users are ass=
igned points for completing tasks or challenges, and whoever has the most p=
oints is at the top of the leaderboard. Figure 1 shows an example of a mobi=
le game leaderboard. The leaderboard shows the ranking of the leading compe=
titors and also displays the position of the user on it.</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
