ach team. Each row begins with a star; the color of the star changes from r=
ed to light pink as the rank decreases.  The 'Rank' column shows the numeri=
cal position (1, 2, 3, 4). The 'Player' column lists the team names: Aquabo=
ys, B team, Berlin's Angels, and GrendelTeam.  The 'Points' column displays=
 the corresponding score for each team: 976, 956, 890, and 878 respectively=
.  The data is arranged in descending order of points, with the highest-sco=
ring team at the top.  There are no connections or information flow between=
 the rows; each row represents an independent entry in the leaderboard." wi=
dth=3D"500" height=3D"202" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"1" src=3D"https:=
