beled 'scatter-gather' indicate that data from each of the three shard tabl=
es is sent to a central 'top 10' table. This table aggregates the top 10 en=
tries across all shards, based on the score, resulting in a combined list o=
f the top 10 members with their corresponding scores.  The 'top 10' table a=
lso has 'score' and 'member' columns, mirroring the structure of the shard =
tables.  The process implies a distributed system where data is initially p=
artitioned across multiple shards, then consolidated to produce an overall =
top 10 ranking." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"500" height=3D"540" decoding=3D"=
